Traditional operating systems often depend on fixed heuristics and manually de
signed rules for task scheduling, limiting their adaptability to dynamic and hetero
geneous workloads. We present a model that first employs supervised learning to
 mimic existing schedulers, followed by reinforcement learning to optimize key
 performance metrics. Transformer encoders are integrated to capture contextual
 relationships among competing tasks, enabling more informed and adaptive priori
tization decisions. This paper introduces a novel hybrid approach that leverages
 attention mechanisms and a two-phase learning strategy to overcome these lim
itations. TITAN’s hybrid approach significantly enhances scheduling efficiency,
 demonstrating its potential to transform resource management in real-time systems.
 This work establishes a foundation for intelligent, context-aware, and learning
based resource management, providing a compelling alternative to traditional
 rule-based scheduling policies across domains such as real-time systems, cloud
 computing, and distributed networks
